  "theme": "work",
  "culturalNote": "Job interviews in Kenya are usually in English, but switching to Swahili for a question or two is a great way to show respect and build rapport — especially with a Kenyan team. Talking about your experience is where continuous tenses shine: \"nimekuwa nikifanya kazi…\" (I have been working…), \"nilipokuwa nikisoma…\" (when I was studying…). Purpose clauses use ili + subjunctive: \"ili nijifunze\" (so that I learn).",
  "startingPoint": "You're interviewing for a manager role at a Nairobi tech company. The HR lead, Mrs Kamau, starts in Swahili.",
